WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.585
Microsoft Learn's page, Connect machines
to Azure Arc at scale with Ansible,

2
00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:07.292
documents onboarding through the Azure Arc

3
00:00:07.292 --> 00:00:09.925
onboarding role in the
azure az collection.

4
00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:14.013
It installs the Connected Machine
agent and registers each host.

5
00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:18.343
The repository keeps a pinned copy
of the role's code, from the ansible

6
00:00:18.343 --> 00:00:22.674
collections azure repository at the
four point two point oh release.

7
00:00:22.674 --> 00:00:26.650
Running it offline, and reading its
code, shows what it leaves to you.

8
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.732
It connects whatever
hosts the inventory names;

9
00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:33.200
the kit reads both owners and
writes them into the tags.

10
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.075
It has no waves; the kit adds a wave
column, one canary server, then five,

11
00:00:38.075 --> 00:00:43.212
then twenty-five percent, and keeps
production out of waves zero and one.

12
00:00:43.212 --> 00:00:46.390
It can't run in check mode on
a server without the agent;

13
00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.712
the kit's playbook doesn't call
it without a confirm flag.

14
00:00:49.712 --> 00:00:54.130
The role's code sends a signal with
the subscription and tenant by default,

15
00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:57.462
which Learn's page doesn't
mention; the kit turns that off.

16
00:00:57.462 --> 00:01:00.171
And it leaves no record,
and the requirements

17
00:01:00.171 --> 00:01:03.100
file on Learn's page
installs the latest version.

18
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.576
The verdict, which is this workbook's:

19
00:01:05.576 --> 00:01:09.600
use Microsoft's role, unchanged,
and add what sits around it.
